[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995054579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995054579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995054579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yhOfz","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T06:09:30Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T06:09:30Z","body":"This error tells you that the object was deleted while its own signal handler was executing (`await` coroutines are implemented with a one-shot signal handler, the rest of the `_ready()` function becomes a one-shot signal handler for `t.test`).\n\nAs far as I can tell, this is not supported behavior. All signal handlers are supposed to complete before the object is deleted.\n\nYou can try to work around the issue as suggested in the error text, or add `await get_tree().process_frame` before `t = null`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995054579/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995070780","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995070780","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995070780,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yhSc8","user":{"login":"Daylily-Zeleen","id":61624558,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNjI0NTU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61624558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen","html_url":"https://github.com/Daylily-Zeleen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T06:17:17Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T06:18:09Z","body":"This is not occur in previous version, such as 4.4.1 stable.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/99790487-e9e2-4ddf-a26d-25c963a2d52a)\nYou can see not any error in debugger.\n\n------------\n\nIntuitively, signal emitting is finished after `await` is executed, delete the object should be safe.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995070780/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995083657","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995083657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995083657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yhVmJ","user":{"login":"Daylily-Zeleen","id":61624558,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNjI0NTU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61624558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen","html_url":"https://github.com/Daylily-Zeleen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Daylily-Zeleen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T06:23:01Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T06:23:01Z","body":"The point is not `t = null`, it just help us to catch the error that where it is occurred in script.\nThis error will occur event if we remove this line.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995083657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995278197","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995278197","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995278197,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yiFF1","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T07:35:33Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T07:35:33Z","body":"> The point is not `t = null`, it just help us to catch the error that where it is occurred in script.\n> This error will occur event if we remove this line.\n\nYes, there is no difference here, because otherwise the local variable will be cleared at the end of the function.\n\n> Intuitively, signal emitting is finished after `await` is executed\n\nNo, the intuitive expectation here is wrong. The signal handler execution ends when the call is interrupted (reaches the end, `return` or `await` signal/coroutine). `await get_tree().process_frame` fixes the problem precisely by delaying the object dereferencing after the signal handler has completed.\n\n> delete the object should be safe\n\nMaybe, if it really is a regression. Bisection is needed to determine the cause.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995278197/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995597448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995597448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995597448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yjTCI","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T09:07:24Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T09:07:24Z","body":"> Maybe, if it really is a regression. Bisection is needed to determine the cause.\n\nBisects to #105453.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995597448/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995651680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995651680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995651680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yjgRg","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T09:25:15Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T09:25:15Z","body":"@reduz @RandomShaper @AThousandShips What do you think, is this a regression or a fix for some undefined behavior that is unfortunately more intuitively expected?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995651680/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995657821","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995657821","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995657821,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yjhxd","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T09:27:31Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T09:27:31Z","body":"I think this is a necessary limitation to prevent leaks, I suspect the signal connection doesn't keep the object alive specifically to prevent circular references, but I'm not sure but that would be my immediate guess","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995657821/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995678738","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107859#issuecomment-2995678738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107859","id":2995678738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yjm4S","user"